      "content": "Those are really helpful for the module. I want to push this a bit further for the \"Advanced Bias\" section. \n\nIn some of the case studies we're building, we want to explore if there's a difference in how these candidates are actually *ranked* in a scorecard. If you had to create a hypothetical scoring breakdown for a \"Project Manager\" role, how would a biased manager likely score them on \"Leadership Potential\" and \"Communication Clarity\"? \n\nFor example, would they give the Midwestern candidate a 9/10 for clarity and the others lower? I need to show that these biases aren't just vague feelings, but they actually lead to lower numerical scores for certain groups.",
